{title: Angels We Have Heard on High}
{artist: Traditional French carol}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Carol}
{key: G}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 125장}
{title_ko: 천사들의 노래가}
{score: angels-we-have-heard-on-high.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Angels we have [D]heard on high
[G]Sweetly singing [D]o'er the [G]plains
And the [G]mountains in [D]reply
[G]Echoing their [D]joyous [G]strains
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Glo__[Em]__[Am]__[D]__[G]__[C]__[D]__ria
In [G/B]ex[D]cel[G]sis [C]De[D]o
[G]Glo__[Em]__[Am]__[D]__[G]__[C]__[D]__ria
In [G/B]ex[D]cel[G]sis [C]De[D]o[G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Shepherds, why this [D]jubilee
[G]Why your joyous [D]strains pro[G]long
What the [G]gladsome tidings [D]be
[G]Which inspire your [D]heavenly [G]song
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Come to Bethlehem and [D]see
[G]Him whose birth the [D]angels [G]sing
Come a[G]dore on bended [D]knee
[G]Christ the Lord, the [D]newborn [G]King
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
